Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 02:08:26 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] SourbyCraft - drop cancelled tasks when splitting a region
 task queue

Cancelling a queued region task only clears its reference count; the
task stays in the queue until polled. Its chunk ticket is released, so
its section can unload. A later split of that queue then looked the
task's section up among the new regions, found none and threw
IllegalStateException under the regioniser's write lock, which stops
the server. A task without a reference count can never run, so split
now drops it instead of routing it.

diff --git a/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/RegionizedTaskQueue.java b/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/RegionizedTaskQueue.java
index aed1a307b1d946a465fbba124de5edf8c674cfce..e66ce540744b9a93d0505dbb875d5e55d5009a1c 100644
--- a/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/RegionizedTaskQueue.java
+++ b/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/RegionizedTaskQueue.java
@@ -391,6 +391,12 @@ public final class RegionizedTaskQueue {
                     final ArrayDeque<ChunkBasedPriorityTask> fromQ = thisQueues[i];
 
                     for (final ChunkBasedPriorityTask task : fromQ) {
+                        // SourbyCraft start - drop a cancelled or completed task instead of routing it: it holds no
+                        // reference count, so its section may have unloaded, and it would never run anyway
+                        if (task.getReferenceCounterVolatile() == null) {
+                            continue;
+                        }
+                        // SourbyCraft end - drop a cancelled or completed task instead of routing it
                         final int sectionX = task.chunkX >> shift;
                         final int sectionZ = task.chunkZ >> shift;
                         final long sectionKey = CoordinateUtils.getChunkKey(sectionX, sectionZ);
